// aug14f hz0 generate divergence_000000, minimized 12.6KB -> ~250B
// (2026-08-15). INTERP-side, the MapQ face of the standing-bottoms
// genus ("standing bottoms never re-fire" — the aug13k fold-init /
// depth-trip / select-miss family; FoldQ got its triggering/standing
// split, MapQ's finish never did). A slot's taint mark is PERSISTENT
// (set once by a triggering bottom, cleared only by a clean
// production), and the finish minted FRESH_BOTTOM on ANY production
// while any slot carried it — so a find over a permanently-bottoming
// predicate (`re::is_match` with an invalid pattern, `$`-dropped) fed
// by a PASS_THROUGH source ride re-delivered FreshBottom every cycle.
// The triggering delivery drove the guard-select downstream and the
// outer select emitted on a cycle where nothing it consumed fired
// (the ref-write block exists only to give the program a second
// cycle; the earlier "ref-write wake" reading was wrong — GXDBG_CS
// showed the callback riding stale while the find's CS-RES stayed
// Tag(64)). Fix: both bottom mints in MapQ's finish gate on
// tag.triggers(); a quiet production over standing poison rides
// (StaleBottom).
{let v47: [bool, null] = array::find([true, true, true], |v21| re::is_match(#pat: "((", "a")$); {let v61 = i64:3; let v67 = &v61; *v67 <- i64:0}; select i64:0 {i64:7 if select v47 {null as _ => false, bool as n => n} => true, v91 => true}}
